libc++ <tuple>: member typedef _BaseT unknown during tuple_element
instantiation, cascading to 'no match for get'; a direct
friend-get replica passes, needs the real header machinery.
Update 2026-07-24: the _BaseT chain is FIXED (__make_integer_seq +
__type_pack_element clang builtin alias templates; member alias
templates now bind the enclosing specialization's arguments).  The
residual is std::get<I>(tuple&): all four overloads are rejected --
the return type `typename tuple_element<_Ip, tuple<_Tp...>>::type&`
